  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nThursday looks to be the warmest day of the week, with \nincreasing southerly flow ahead of the next system. Temperatures\non Thursday will be 10-15 degrees above normal, with lower \nelevation max temps around the around 90 degrees and around 80 \ndegrees in mountain valleys. Come Friday, a trough and it's \nassociated cold front will move across the region, ushering in \nbreezy winds and cooler temperatures. Right now our northern \nzones (Baker and Valley counties) have the best chances of \nprecipitation with this front (15-30% chance), otherwise the \nfrontal passage will be rather dry. Long-range guidance is in \ngood agreement on the front making it's way through the area \nFriday/Friday night. This will allow for temperatures near or \naround 5 degrees below normal this weekend into the start of \nnext week.",
